<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Bosnia</h1><p class="st-meta">1377 CE – 1463 CE · capital Bobovac</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Medieval Bosnian kingdom of the Kotromanić dynasty, briefly the strongest Balkan state, until the Ottomans conquered it in 1463.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Ban <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tvrtko-i-of-bosnia">Tvrtko I</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/banate-of-bosnia">Banate of Bosnia</a>, having won lands in western <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/serbia">Serbia</a>, was crowned king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a> in 1377 at Mile near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visoko">Visoko</a>, claiming descent from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nemanjic-dynasty">Nemanjić dynasty</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tvrtko-i-of-bosnia">Tvrtko</a> expanded to the Adriatic, taking <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-kotor">Kotor</a> and much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a> by his death in 1391. Royal power then weakened as great nobles such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hrvoje-vukcic-hrvatinic">Hrvoje Vukčić Hrvatinić</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stjepan-vukcic-kosaca">Stjepan Vukčić Kosača</a>, whose lands became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herzegovina">Herzegovina</a>, made and unmade kings. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">Silver</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srebrenica">Srebrenica</a> supported the state, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnian-church">Bosnian Church</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a> and Orthodoxy coexisted. Carved tombstones called stećci mark the burials of the period.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> took parts of the kingdom from the 1430s. In 1463 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-ii">Mehmed II</a> invaded, captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bobovac">Bobovac</a> and executed the last king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stephen-tomasevic">Stephen Tomašević</a>, at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jajce">Jajce</a>. Most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a> became an Ottoman province, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> held a northern banate around Jajce until 1527.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-bosnia.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Bosnia" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Sci Show With Moh / Vectorization: Mrmw · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Banner_of_King_Tvrtko_I_of_Bosnia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1377 CE – 1463 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bobovac</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Tvrtko I, Stephen Tomaš, Stephen Tomašević</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Bosnian Church; Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Bosnian (Serbian-Croatian)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/bosnia-and-herzegovina">Bosnia and Herzegovina</a>, <a href="/countries/croatia">Croatia</a>, <a href="/countries/montenegro">Montenegro</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bosnian Kingdom, Kotromanić Bosnia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1420&amp;focus=kingdom-of-bosnia" aria-label="Kingdom of Bosnia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5117 615 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Bosnia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5437 871L5437 871M5437 871L5709 970M5437 871L5369 838M5437 871L5396 891M5437 871L5455 925"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5437 871h0M5709 970h0M5369 838h0